course: dictionary
lesson: 14253
title: One word, more than one meaning
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. Nerves is one of them. To find the right meaning, read the words around it, because they are its context and they leave clues.
explain: «Her nerves got the better of her before the spelling test.» The test tells you that nerves here means the worried, jittery feeling you get before something important. Ask: what word would fit here? Then try your meaning in the sentence and check it still makes sense.
explain: Nerves in your body are thin fibres that carry messages between your brain and the rest of you. «When he touched the hot pan, the nerves in his hand sent a message to his brain, and he pulled away fast.» That is the body meaning. Nerves of steel is a third meaning: staying calm in a hard moment.
fact: Nerves are thin fibres in your body that carry messages between your brain and other parts of your body.
fact: «Nerves» can also mean the worried, nervous feeling you get before something important, like a test or a show.
fact: «Nerves of steel» means courage to stay calm in a hard moment.
fact: «Get on someone's nerves» means to annoy them, and «lose your nerve» means to become too scared to carry on.
fact: Deep breathing can help you calm your nerves before a performance or a test.
exercise: «The actor had nerves before she walked on to the stage.» What does nerves mean here? | *The worried feeling before something important | Courage to stay calm in a hard moment | Thin fibres that carry messages in the body | Parts of a plant
exercise: The doctor explained that nerves carry messages from your skin to your brain. What are nerves? | Bones that protect the brain | *Thin fibres that carry messages around the body | Calm feelings after a long day | A worried feeling before a test
exercise: «Jake stayed calm when the lights went out, with nerves of steel.» What does nerves of steel mean? | A strong metal wire | *Courage to stay calm in a hard moment | Feeling sick after lunch | Shouting loudly at everyone
test: «My little brother gets on my nerves when he hums.» What does get on someone's nerves mean? | To go to sleep | To help them with a task | *To annoy them | To make them laugh
test: Find the phrase that shows Amira felt worried before the school play. | a bright red coat | a long walk home | a loud, happy song | *a bag of nerves
exam: When Sam touched the hot kettle, which part of his body sent a message to his brain? | His hair | His favourite book | *The nerves in his hand | His school bag
